    {
      "id": "claim_a2a3d97d4b954ab19ba98bcf102278a5",
      "statement": "An embedded PDF font is a glyph subset: svgToPdf runs a probe pass to collect the used glyph ids, subsetTrueType keeps those glyphs and their composite components (other glyphs get empty outlines, glyph ids stay the same), the subset is deflated, and a second pass writes a Type0 Identity-H font with a ToUnicode CMap so text stays copyable and searchable. If the font cannot be subset, the whole font is embedded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/diagramExport.ts#L70-L78",
